 "phase": "W2b-4c: the browser host from a static host",
 "change": "web_app.py build assembles a folder any static host serves without the runner: index.html (the page), wasi-worker.js, audio.js, config.json, and data-<12 hex of a SHA-256 over every data file>/ with app/NTSDWeb.wasm (the build's, byte for byte), app/NTSDNative_NTSDCore.bundle, music/ and each mount's listing (app.json, music.json: [{path, dir, size}]); _headers (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages) and vercel.json with the isolation headers (COOP same-origin, COEP require-corp, CORP same-origin) and Cache-Control immutable for /data-*; files cloned (cp -c) on APFS. web_app.py serve is a test static server with those headers and a JSON request log; measure reports a session's requests, bytes and compressed sizes. The page reads config.json beside it (the runner serves /web/config.json with runner: true), loads its scripts relative to itself, makes the config's URLs absolute for the worker, and without the runner sends nothing to it: output to the console, a failure, the end or a stop (with the exit code, passed in the frame header) shown to the player, load progress on the notice; a folder path without its slash is redirected. The worker lists a static mount from its manifest and reads files by URL with three tries of 60 s each, falls back to compiling from the bytes when a host does not send application/wasm, and prefetches the /app mount's files 8 at a time while the module compiles — only after a probe shows that the browser's cache serves its synchronous reads (one file fetched, then read; its timing entry must show no transfer). web_run.mjs: config route first; --url URL opens an external page (with --steps in Chromium, ending with 1 when the page's program exited non-zero; or --for SECONDS in any engine).",
