  "note": "--web scripted pages through the runner (the page's config.json path) in Chromium and WebKit; frames compared with tw-w1b3/wasi (the none group); the page, worker, runner and web_app.py unchanged from before the saves check to after the regression (SHA-256 checked)"
 },
 "existingHosts": "No Core, Runtime, Package.swift or Swift change; the program is W2b-3's NTSDWeb.wasm, byte-identical in the static folder",
 "review": "Round 1 (independent, read-only): critical: the runner's /web/ files route answered config.json with 404 before the new config route (every runner run would have failed); high: the page did not tell the worker it ran without the runner (output and the end posted to the static host; a buffered flush in a question could kill the game); medium: a failure looked like a normal end; a real network would need 1,530 one-at-a-time requests revalidated each visit (~75 s of round trips at 50 ms); reads without retry or timeout; low: subpath without a slash, host limits and MIME, TZ, measure counts, clone fallback, --url gaps. Fixed (TZ and console capture documented). Round 2: OK; low items queued: the slash redirect lets the script run on; no progress while the probe skips the prefetch; the prefetch runs on after a startup failure; a one-file probe cannot see later cache eviction; --url exits 0 when the page never started; the immutable rule matches the site root only; page, config and scripts rely on host revalidation defaults; retries without a pause; --url step timing and a save in flight at the last step.",
 "boundaries": [
  "Publishing needs the user; no host was tried",
  "A first visit downloads ~881 MB (the full data, as the original loads it) — the hosting decision (bandwidth, per-file limits) is the user's",
  "The guest runs in UTC on a static page (the runner pins Etc/GMT-1; whether WASI Foundation honours TZ for the player's zone is unchecked)",
  "WebKit (Playwright's build) gets no prefetch; real Safari untried",
  "Deployment at the site root assumed for the immutable rule"
 ]
}